  "body": "The previous text said to not create a strong reference to the promise,\nwhich was incorrect since it means that code like\ncustomElements.whenDefined(\"x-foo\").then(f) might never call f, since\nnothing is keeping the promise alive. So, that needs to be removed.\n\nOnce that is removed, keeping a separate promise around for each call to\nwhenDefined() becomes more expensive. So, instead we create a maximum of\none promise, and return it every time.\n\nThanks @dominiccooney for finding. Could use @annevk review too.\n",
